zig_iroh — third-party notices
================================

This source package includes the patched C dependency trees used by the shipping
picoquic + picotls transport stack:

- picoquic, pinned at 91405da4d966966f74e03ddd89a6bb8be599aa73 — MIT.
  See `deps/picoquic/LICENSE`. Individual retained source files also carry their
  own notices where applicable.
- picotls, pinned at a096f85363edfd9d4f019412232fb6293af504f7 — MIT.
  See `deps/picotls/README.md`.
- cifra, included under picotls — CC0-1.0.
  See `deps/picotls/deps/cifra/COPYING`.
- micro-ecc, included under picotls — BSD-2-Clause.
  See `deps/picotls/deps/micro-ecc/LICENSE.txt`.
- picotls fusion code includes Apache-2.0 and MIT notices in the retained source.

The package links to the host's OpenSSL `libcrypto`; OpenSSL source is not
included. A build host therefore needs compatible OpenSSL development headers
and libraries. The hash-pinned `tls.zig` package remains a Zig package-manager
dependency and may require network access on a cold package cache.

The Zig sources are part of the independent zig_iroh port of iroh and are
available under MIT OR Apache-2.0. See `LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-APACHE`.
Upstream iroh (Rust) is MIT/Apache-2.0 dual-licensed by n0.
